# This repository is PUBLIC, and it will hold an application that reads people's own equipment.
# The rules below are the same ones harmony-explorations enforces, kept in the same order so the
# two files can be compared at a glance. See CLAUDE.md for why each one matters.

# Proprietary Logitech firmware and config binaries. A config is Logitech generated data including
# an infrared database compiled from theirs, so it is a copyright matter and not a privacy one, and
# a remote's info output carries serial GUIDs, which is the privacy one. Share checksums, not files.
# Listed before this repository holds a single test fixture, because the first fixture anybody
# reaches for is exactly one of these.
*.bin
*.hfw
*.EZHex
*.EZUp
*.EzHex
*.EzUpgrade
*-info.txt

# Rendered screens and anything else drawn from somebody's config. A picture of a remote's screen
# is a picture of their equipment list.
screens/
renders/

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. They accumulate absolute paths from whoever's machine they
# were written on. Shared configuration belongs in .claude/settings.json, which is committed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Node and Electron. A lock file is committed on purpose, since dependencies are pinned exactly in
# package.json and the lock file pins the transitive tree the same way.
node_modules/
dist/
out/
release/
*.tsbuildinfo

# IDE project state. WebStorm's workspace.xml carries local paths and a per-install GUID.
.idea/
.vscode/

# Build and tool noise.
.DS_Store
*.log

# Screenshots of the window, which are for looking at rather than for keeping.
var/
